    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>lasch (redlash): a fine kind of leather, usually red but also black, cordovan, used for covering furniture, for bookbinding and for clothing (Cobb 185; OED s.v. lasch; see also cordwain).</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
